Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:33:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] tabletmanager: configure a chosen source that the shard
 record names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Once a request chose a source, the retry only waited for replication to
run from it. If the request failed before starting replication, or timed
out on a restore's action lock after which the restore reset replication,
nothing configured that source again, and the replica stayed NOT_SERVING
until another request came.

When replication does not run from the chosen source and the shard record
names it, initialize replication from it under the shard lock, with
initialization's checks. If the record names another tablet, keep waiting,
so that a stale record never replaces the choice.

Signed-off-by: Miguel Ángel Pastor Olivar <migue@planetscale.com>
---
 .../replication_initialization_test.go        | 67 +++++++++++++++++--
 go/vt/vttablet/tabletmanager/tm_init.go       | 39 +++++++++--
 2 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

